{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6824116","formula":"C₁₀H₁₃NO₃","hill":"C10H13NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":13.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Metirosine"},"descriptions":{"en":"α-Methyl-p-tyrosine (AMPT), or simply α-methyltyrosine, also known in its chiral 2-(S) form as metirosine, is a tyrosine hydroxylase enzyme inhibitor and is therefore a drug involved in inhibiting the catecholamine biosynthetic pathway. AMPT inhibits tyrosine hydroxylase whose enzymatic activity is normally regulated through the phosphorylation of different serine residues in regulatory domain sites. Catecholamine biosynthesis starts with dietary tyrosine, which is hydroxylated by tyrosine hydroxylase and it is hypothesized that AMPT competes with tyrosine at the tyrosine-binding site, causing inhibition of tyrosine hydroxylase."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":441350,"mass":195.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@](CC1=CC=C(C=C1)O)(C(=O)O)N","inchikey":"NHTGHBARYWONDQ-JTQLQIEISA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-amino-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-2-methylpropanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"441350","atoms":27,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.422,"y":1.312,"z":1.422,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.758,"y":1.788,"z":-0.338,"el":"O"},{"x":4.286,"y":0.511,"z":0.496,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.373,"y":-0.912,"z":-0.579,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.071,"y":-0.532,"z":-0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.966,"y":-0.852,"z":-1.048,"el":"C"},{"x":0.442,"y":-0.486,"z":-0.633,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.903,"y":-1.352,"z":1.277,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.136,"y":0.962,"z":0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":0.931,"y":0.772,"z":-0.937,"el":"C"},{"x":1.212,"y":-1.419,"z":0.04,"el":"C"},{"x":2.23,"y":1.109,"z":-0.556,"el":"C"},{"x":2.51,"y":-1.083,"z":0.422,"el":"C"},{"x":3.019,"y":0.181,"z":0.124,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.99,"y":-1.921,"z":-1.305,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.188,"